    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG proudly introduces 5 Botanic Mews, an attractive red brick home, presented in pristine condition and situated in this quiet and highly sought after residential setting in the heart of Glasnevin. The property offers bright, well presented accommodation over three levels, complemented by a private South facing rear garden and an excellent BER rating.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of an entrance hall, living room with feature fireplace and fitted storage, kitchen and dining area with access to the rear courtyard. On the first floor there are two double bedrooms, an ensuite and main shower room. The next level boasts a bright converted attic room with rooflight and eaves storage.\n\nThe location is a particular feature, offering a peaceful residential setting while remaining within easy reach of Glasnevin, Drumcondra and Phibsborough. Excellent outdoor amenities include the National Botanic Gardens, Griffith Park and Albert College Park and the renowned John Kavanagh, The Gravediggers pub, are also close by.\n\nThe area is particularly well served by schools, including Glasnevin National School, St.Vincent's Primary School, St. Vincent's Secondary School, St. Mary's Secondary School and Scoil Chaitríona. Dublin City University, including its Glasnevin and St Patrick's campuses, are also easily accessible.\n\nThe property enjoys convenient access to Dublin city centre, while Dublin Airport, the M1 and M50 are only a short drive away. The combination of a quiet setting with excellent schools, parks, third level education, transport links and established local amenities makes this a particularly convenient location.\n\nFor further details please contact DNG Phibsboro on 01 8300989 Local agents Michelle Keeley MIPAV MMCEP, Ciaran Jones MIPAV, Brian McGee MIPAV, Isabel O Neill MIPAV, Vincent Mullen MIPAV and Leah Barry."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nExterior: - \nAttractive red brick terraced residence with a traditional facade, main hall door with glass panels inset and an overhanging porch roof. The property presents neatly to the street with low maintenance frontage and benefits from convenient parking outside the front door.\n\nEntrance Hall: - 1.57m x 1.20m\nWelcoming entrance hall provides access to the ground floor accommodation, with timber flooring and stairs leading to the upper floor.\n\nKitchen / Living / Dining Room: - 7.20m x 3.94m\nThe property features a bright and spacious open plan kitchen, dining and living area, creating a comfortable and practical main living space. The kitchen offers a range of wall and floor units with ample worktop space and tiled splashback, while the adjoining dining area features timber flooring and glazed doors which allow natural light to fill the room and provide direct access to the rear courtyard.The living area continues the timber flooring and benefits from good natural light from the front window. A feature fireplace provides an attractive focal point, complemented by convenient shelving and storage units, together with ceiling coving.\n\nStairs and Landing: - \nBright landing area with a carpeted staircase, painted timber balustrade and natural light from the adjoining rooms. The landing provides access to the first floor accommodation and continues on to the stairs up to the converted attic level.\n\nBedroom 1: - 2.79m max x 3.90m\nThe first double bedroom is beautifully presented and offers a rear aspect, carpeted flooring and a window providing natural light. The room is well proportioned with space for bedside furniture and presents with two double fitted wardrobe discreetly tucked away.\n\nEn-Suite - 0.68m x 1.41m\nThe ensuite comprises of a wash hand basin and WC. Fitted vanity storage provides a useful additional space, with a wall mounted mirror and window providing natural light and ventilation.\n\nBedroom 2: - 2.54m x 3.90m\nThis bright and well presented second double bedroom has a lovely front aspect and offers stylish carpeted flooring and two bright windows providing good natural light. The room also benefits from built in double wardrobes, with generous storage.\n\nShower Room: - 1.52m x 1.92m\nThe fully tiled shower room comprises of a glazed shower enclosure, wash hand basin and WC. The room also includes fitted vanity storage and a wall mounted mirror.\n\nAttic Room: - 3.63m x 3.90m\nThe attic has been converted into additional living accommodation with a large skylight providing excellent natural light. The room is finished with carpet flooring and includes recessed ceiling lighting, a wall mounted radiator and useful storage within the eaves.\n\nSouth facing Garden: - \nThe private rear garden offers a private and low maintenance outdoor space. The garden comes fully paved with timber boundary fencing. There is ample space for outdoor seating and potted plants, with direct access from the house through glazed double doors.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Quiet residential setting in the heart of Glasnevin</li><li> Bright open plan kitchen, dining and living area</li><li> Private enclosed rear courtyard</li><li> Excellent B BER energy rating</li><li> Converted attic room with rooflight and eaves storage</li><li> En suite</li><li> National Botanic Gardens, Griffith Park and Albert College Park are on your doorstep.</li><li> Excellent choice of primary and secondary schools nearby</li><li> Convenient to DCU Glasnevin and St Patrick's campuses</li><li> Close to Bon Secours Hospital</li><li> Easy access to Dublin city centre, M50 and Dublin Airport</li><li> Within easy reach of Glasnevin, Drumcondra and Phibsborough</li><li> Excellent local cafés, shops, restaurants and amenities, including The Gravediggers pub</ul>"
      },
